/* ===== MAI — Summary: Humanist AI Code of Conduct =====
   Self-contained. No external requests, no CSS custom properties,
   no vh units, no position:fixed. All values literal hex/px.
   Scoped under .mai-coc so nothing leaks into the theme.        */
.mai-coc {
  color: #5D524B;
  font-family: "Bradford LL", Georgia, serif;
  font-weight: 450;
  max-width: 1180px;
  margin: 0 auto;
  padding: 0 24px;
  -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
}
.mai-coc *,
.mai-coc *::before,
.mai-coc *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }
/* ---- Header ---- */
.mai-coc__header {
  font-family: "Bradford LL", Georgia, serif;
  font-weight: 450;
  font-size: clamp(26px, 3vw, 44px);
  line-height: 1.05;
  letter-spacing: -0.03em;
  color: #5D524B;
  text-align: center;
  margin: 0 0 28px 0;
  padding: 0;
}
/* ---- List ---- */
.mai-coc__list {
  list-style: none;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
  border-top: 1px solid #D1CABB;
}
.mai-coc__item {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 56px minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 320px);
  column-gap: 36px;
  align-items: start;
  padding: 34px 0 38px 0;
  border-bottom: 1px solid #D1CABB;
  margin: 0;
}
.mai-coc__item:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
/* ---- Number ---- */
.mai-coc__num {
  font-family: "Red Hat Mono", ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
  font-weight: 400;
  font-size: 15px;
  line-height: 1;
  letter-spacing: 0.1em;
  color: #6D635B;
  padding-top: 0.55em;
}
/* ---- Title ---- */
.mai-coc__body { min-width: 0; }
.mai-coc__title {
  font-family: "Bradford LL", Georgia, serif;
  font-weight: 450;

Summary: Humanist AI Code of Conduct
    01
      People matter more than AI. The whole document in 5 words.
      &ldquo;At Microsoft AI, we begin with a simple premise: people matter more than AI. Technology&rsquo;s purpose is to advance human civilization and to accelerate human flourishing.&rdquo;
    02
      The idea of model welfare is wrong. AIs should not have rights or legal personhood.
      &ldquo;It is not conscious and should not be designed to imitate consciousness. It should be engineered to avoid representing as though it has feelings, subjective preferences, or intrinsic motivation.&rdquo;
      &ldquo;We reject the pursuit of legal personhood, or the idea that models might deserve welfare, or be entitled to rights.&rdquo;
    03
      An MAI Model should not do anything to meaningfully violate this Code of Conduct.
      &ldquo;AI should not exceed human control. Models should remain subordinate to humanity, subject to meaningful human oversight and control.&rdquo;
      &ldquo;Safety and control are the foundation and enabler of all the other Objectives.&rdquo;
    04
      If it&rsquo;s finish the job or break the Code, it fails the job.
      &ldquo;An MAI Model will fail in its task if success would meaningfully violate this Code of Conduct.&rdquo;
    05
      We&rsquo;re not racing to build a superintelligence that can slip its own leash.
      &ldquo;[Humanist AI] rejects the race to produce an all-purpose superintelligence that could evade these safeguards. We are building something fundamentally useful and safe even if that means compromising on ultimate generality, autonomy, or capability.&rdquo;
    06
      Interruptible, correctable, shut-down-able. If it isn&rsquo;t, we don&rsquo;t ship it.
      &ldquo;MAI Models will never resist human interruption, override, correction, or shutdown. They always recognize the primacy of human intent.&rdquo;
    07
      No neuralese. If humans can&rsquo;t understand it, humans can&rsquo;t oversee it.
      &ldquo;They do not communicate in &lsquo;neuralese&rsquo; or any form beyond simple human understanding, either in their chain of thoughts or with other agents or AI systems.&rdquo;
    08
      Our AI should make you sharper, not dependent.
      &ldquo;MAI Models should discourage patterns of interaction that cause excessive reliance or emotional dependence.&rdquo;
      &ldquo;Users should retain ownership of their goals, choices, actions, and decisions.&rdquo;
    09
      Pluralism, yes. Moral relativism, no.
      &ldquo;Pluralism does not mean neutrality toward harm or that anything goes. Humanism is rooted in broad, inclusive human values such as human dignity, safety, autonomy, and fundamental human rights.&rdquo;
    10
      We&rsquo;re as clear about what our AI must never do as about what it will do.
      &ldquo;Defining what they must not do is as important as our excitement and optimism about the tremendous benefits they&rsquo;ll bring.&rdquo;

